WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.892 --> 00:00:03.736 line:90%
NARRATOR: <i>How much would
it cost to be a wizard</i>

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:05.741 line:90%
<i>at Hogwarts like Harry Potter?</i>

00:00:05.741 --> 00:00:06.741 line:90%
<i>Let's find out.</i>

00:00:06.741 --> 00:00:09.344 line:10%
<i>You just got your acceptance letter
to Hogwarts</i>

00:00:09.344 --> 00:00:12.585 line:10%
<i>and you're extremely excited,
but you need to get the checkbook out</i>

00:00:12.585 --> 00:00:14.520 line:90%
<i>because it's going to pricey.</i>

00:00:14.520 --> 00:00:18.025 line:90%
<i>If you're a true Potterhead, you know
that J.K. Rowling has declared that</i>

00:00:18.025 --> 00:00:21.823 line:10%
<i>Hogwarts tuition is free because the
Ministry of Magic covers the costs,</i>

00:00:21.823 --> 00:00:24.383 line:10%
<i>so the seven years you'll spend
studying at Hogwarts will be</i>

00:00:24.383 --> 00:00:27.354 line:10%
<i>completely free, unlike my education.</i>

00:00:27.354 --> 00:00:29.689 line:90%
<i>Hogwarts tuition $0.</i>

00:00:29.689 --> 00:00:32.631 line:10%
<i>You're going to need to get
some wizard school supplies</i>

00:00:32.631 --> 00:00:35.068 line:10%
<i>and there's no better place than
the theme park gift shop.</i>

00:00:35.068 --> 00:00:36.578 line:10%
<i>I mean Diagon Alley.</i>

00:00:36.578 --> 00:00:38.783 line:10%
<i>According to the Hogwarts
acceptance letter,</i>

00:00:38.783 --> 00:00:41.322 line:10%
<i>students are required to buy
many things ranging from</i>

00:00:41.322 --> 00:00:43.130 line:10%
<i>a winter cloak to a pewter cauldron.</i>

00:00:43.130 --> 00:00:46.013 line:90%
<i>These items cost $1,031.</i>

00:00:46.013 --> 00:00:47.358 line:10%
<i>Do you want a magical pet?</i>

00:00:47.358 --> 00:00:51.338 line:10%
<i>Most bird breeders will charge
about $250 for an owl adoption.</i>

00:00:51.338 --> 00:00:54.454 line:10%
<i>Add on some veterinarian costs, food,
a nice cage,</i>

00:00:54.454 --> 00:00:56.144 line:90%
<i>we get to $400.</i>

00:00:56.144 --> 00:00:57.833 line:10%
<i>But how about transportation?</i>

00:00:57.833 --> 00:00:59.781 line:90%
<i>Go to platform nine
and three-quarters</i>

00:00:59.781 --> 00:01:01.572 line:90%
<i>and board the Hogwarts express.</i>

00:01:01.572 --> 00:01:04.282 line:10%
<i>The average train ride
going that distance in England</i>

00:01:04.282 --> 00:01:06.214 line:10%
<i>is about $150.</i>

00:01:06.214 --> 00:01:08.462 line:10%
<i>Now that you're living in Hogwarts,
you'll want to dive into</i>

00:01:08.462 --> 00:01:10.733 line:10%
<i>some of the local activities
like Quidditch.</i>

00:01:10.733 --> 00:01:13.160 line:10%
<i>To play this awesome game, you need
your own equipment.</i>

00:01:13.160 --> 00:01:16.057 line:90%
<i>A broom, some personal goggles,
and a pair of socks.</i>

00:01:16.057 --> 00:01:18.491 line:10%
<i>The rest is mostly covered
by Hogwarts.</i>

00:01:18.491 --> 00:01:20.728 line:90%
<i>Quidditch $550.</i>

00:01:20.728 --> 00:01:23.757 line:90%
<i>Wizards break a lot of things
in their time at Hogwarts.</i>

00:01:23.757 --> 00:01:27.277 line:90%
<i>Unfortunately, they break a lot
of expensive things.</i>

00:01:27.277 --> 00:01:32.156 line:90%
<i>Costs of damages $6,945,035.</i>

00:01:32.156 --> 00:01:35.476 line:10%
<i>And at the end of a long
stressful day of fighting evil,</i>

00:01:35.476 --> 00:01:37.528 line:10%
<i>you’re going to want to go
to the local pub and have</i>

00:01:37.528 --> 00:01:39.493 line:10%
<i>a delicious butter beer
with your friends.</i>

00:01:39.493 --> 00:01:41.526 line:90%
<i>One round of butter beer is $10.</i>

00:01:41.526 --> 00:01:43.547 line:90%
<i>To calculate the grand total,
we considered that you</i>

00:01:43.547 --> 00:01:45.983 line:90%
<i>spend seven years at Hogwarts
and the inflation value</i>

00:01:45.983 --> 00:01:47.838 line:90%
<i>the British pound changes
over those seven years.</i>

00:01:47.838 --> 00:01:50.362 line:10%
<i>So, converted into wizard money
then converted back into dollars</i>

00:01:50.362 --> 00:01:53.025 line:10%
<i>then factor in structural
macroeconomics, bank loan fees,</i>

00:01:53.025 --> 00:01:54.910 line:10%
<i>national fiscal policies,
you know stuff like that</i>

00:01:54.910 --> 00:02:00.835 line:90%
<i>and it gets us to $15,360,122.</i>

00:02:00.835 --> 00:02:02.385 line:10%
<i>If you want to afford it all,</i>

00:02:02.385 --> 00:02:05.211 line:10%
<i>better be friendly with those goblins
at Gringotts bank</i>

00:02:05.211 --> 00:02:07.867 line:90%
<i>or talk to J.K. Rowling.
She is loaded.</i>

